            <ArticleTitle>[The diagnosis of occupational myofibrosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The studies proved that ultrasound and enhanced roentgenomyography are diagnostic methods of choice for occupational myofibrosis, detecting the lesions as well as their extent and severity. Comparing diagnostic value of clinical and radiologic methods proved the latter to disclose early signs of the disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
